**Type call: Enneagram 3w2, Social subtype. Confidence high.**

**Core tension:** he sells stability under a name that promises it, while his whole nervous system is wired to a live counter that reports, every few seconds, how many people just left. His father left when he was a kid.

**The material that carries it:**
- **The hook** — 2022, ten thousand people waiting for him, and he stayed in bed. Because it had been thirty thousand before.
- **Named tiebreaker (3 over 7)** — after Bradley Martyn slapped him on camera, he called it "part of the narrative" that boosted his *relevancy*. A Seven files humiliation as a story. He filed it as positioning.
- **Signature detail** — he gave his mother $250,000 to retire on stream in Sept 2024, then took it back in 2026 to cover damages to the ex-FaZe house. On stream. "This was the happiest she's been in years... and I was like, I appreciate that, but I need that $250k back."
- **Bespoke section form** — "The Receipts," a dated purchase ledger (house at 17 → GT3 → the $250k → the clawback) that only works with his receipts.
- **Ending** — 2024 he said "I don't even think Kai likes me anymore." July 2026 at Streamer University, Kai told him why he used to lurk at 2,000 viewers: the blue headset, the dark room, the shoes on the floor. Kai remembered the shoes.

**Verification I ran:** pulled the full 98-minute *All Grown Up* Ep. 10 transcript (Sept 2024) and worked from it directly — several quotes in circulation are host lines, and I discarded the ones I couldn't attribute cleanly (the podcast is FaZe Rug's, and his liquor-store/23andMe material blurs into Ronaldo's in the auto-transcript).

